On the western side of the Le Morne peninsula, the public beach is one of the most beautiful on the island: fine white sand, a lagoon of clear, shallow water and the cliffs of Le Morne Brabant rising directly behind it.

The lagoon off the peninsula is also one of the world's best-known places for kitesurfing, so on windy days the sky fills with kites further along the shore.

Just inland from the beach stands the Slave Route Monument.

## Good to know

- Shade is limited: bring a parasol or come early or late in the day.
- Kitesurfers use parts of the lagoon — swim where others swim, away from their launch areas.
